WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.654
For each protected address the check reads

2
00:00:02.654 --> 00:00:05.475
its diagnostic settings
and the metric alerts.

3
00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:09.862
A log counts if one of Learn's
three DDoS categories, or all logs,

4
00:00:09.862 --> 00:00:13.990
goes to the platform workspace;
Learn says the mitigation

5
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.775
reports category retires
from about mid-August 2026.

6
00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:22.385
An alert counts if it's enabled, has a
criterion on the under-attack metric,

7
00:00:22.385 --> 00:00:26.687
and its scope is the address, its
resource group or its subscription.

8
00:00:26.687 --> 00:00:32.594
That gives six rules: unprotected,
unresolvable, on a NAT gateway, no logs,

9
00:00:32.594 --> 00:00:38.860
no alert, and more than one plan, since
the guide keeps one plan for the agency.
